  "verbalization": "GLPG-0492 is implicated in the biological pathway leading to U373 MG through multiple independent routes. The evidence suggests that GLPG-0492 acts as a target for several compounds, with HEK293 and Ca9-22 being downstream targets in distinct pathways. HEK293 is a target of Woodfordin A and SR-9011, both of which are known to interact with U373 MG, indicating a potential role in the regulation of this cell line. Similarly, Ca9-22 is a target of a compound that also targets U373 MG, suggesting a shared mechanism of action across different compounds. The integration of these pathways implies that GLPG-0492 may influence U373 MG through a common or divergent mechanism, possibly involving cellular signaling or metabolic pathways. The presence of multiple targets and the consistent downstream effect on U373 MG supports a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
